00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:29.600
the contents blowing the entire shuttle apart the&nbsp;
commission's report was highly critical of nasa's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:34.560
leadership for ignoring warnings from engineers&nbsp;
and prioritizing their launch over safety&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:44.000
jaeger's post-retirement years were largely spent&nbsp;
in comfort having amassed a sizable fortune from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:48.160
book royalties endorsement contracts and speaking&nbsp;
engagements jaeger lived with his wife glenis in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:53.200
northern california until she died of ovarian&nbsp;
cancer in 1990 after 45 years of marriage the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:56.720
couple had raised four children together two&nbsp;
of which followed in their father's footsteps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.720 --> 00:14:01.040
with long careers in the air force retirement&nbsp;
didn't put a damper on the old test pilot's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:06.320
thirst for speed however on the 50th anniversary&nbsp;
of jaeger's historic mach 1 flight in 1997 jaeger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:10.560
once again broke the sound barrier piloting an&nbsp;
f15 fighter jet you think that's incredible just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:14.400
considered this wasn't even the last time he'd&nbsp;
do this 15 years later at the eye-popping age&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:19.280
of 89 yeager did it again though on this flight&nbsp;
he consented to make the flight as a passenger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:23.760
the very fact that an 89 year old man would&nbsp;
subject himself to the rigors of supersonic flight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:28.320
says a lot about his character not the jaeger's&nbsp;
golden years were free from controversy however&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:33.360
in 2000 the 77 year old flying ace met and fell&nbsp;
in love with victoria de angelo an actress 35&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:38.320
years as junior in 2003 they married in a private&nbsp;
ceremony the match caused a rift between jaeger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:41.440
and his children who believed that victoria&nbsp;
had only married their father for his money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:45.760
a lawsuit was filed and then a counter suit and&nbsp;
the litigation dragged on for years in the end the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:49.360
court sided with jaeger against his children and&nbsp;
jaeger would tell reporters that he didn't care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:53.440
what his children thought about his life choices&nbsp;
he was going to do whatever he wanted to be happy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:58.320
on december 7 2020 chuck yeager died in los&nbsp;
angeles hospital at the age of 97. the death of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:03.040
this american hero touched off a wave of mourning&nbsp;
nationwide his body was flown aboard air force two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:07.920
the vice president of the united states plane&nbsp;
to charleston west virginia where he was buried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:13.440
with full military honours in a ceremony that took&nbsp;
place on january the 15th 2021 jaeger was so well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:18.400
respected that his funeral briefly brought both&nbsp;
republican and democratic politicians together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:22.320
to pay their respects often called america's&nbsp;
greatest pilot chuck yeager represents the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:27.440
bridge between the rough and tumble aerial cowboys&nbsp;
that typified the fighter pilots of the two world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:32.640
wars with the highly educated technology savvy&nbsp;
professionals that pilot today's modern machines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:37.280
though described by tom wolf as having the right&nbsp;
stuff the combination of guts and daring needed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:42.000
to do things like break the sound barrier and&nbsp;
take other risks jaeger himself disputed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:46.160
he said that his skill in the cockpit could&nbsp;
be attributed to his exceptional vision a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:50.640
thorough knowledge of his airplane and how&nbsp;
it operated and more than a little good luck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:55.040
in any case his contributions to aviation will&nbsp;
long be remembered not only by historians but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:59.600
by military officers space enthusiasts or by&nbsp;
anybody who watches the books and films made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:07.840
about his life and achievements not bad&nbsp;
for a humble farm boy from west virginia

